Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: adapt TB371FC references to Linux 6.12

Linux 6.12.114 has an unlabelled zap-shader child under the SM8250 GPU.
Merge the board firmware-name into that existing child and give it the
board's gpu_zap_shader label, also retaining the label used by the stage0
variant. The inherited memory-region and firmware filename are unchanged.

The DSI PLL output names are private driver defines in this kernel, not
exported DT binding macros. Use output indices 0 (byte) and 1 (pixel), as
provided by dsi_phy_7nm.c and already used by sm8250.dtsi and the upstream
SM8250 Elish board. This changes no selected clock parent or hardware value.

Apply after installing the repository's TB371FC board DTS into the prepared
Linux v6.12.114 source tree. No hardware node or GPIO is removed or guessed.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-tb371fc.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-tb371fc.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-tb371fc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-tb371fc.dts
@@ -497,10 +497,10 @@
 
 &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
-};
-
-&gpu_zap_shader {
-	firmware-name = "qcom/sm8250/lenovo/tb371fc/a650_zap.mbn";
+
+	gpu_zap_shader: zap-shader {
+		firmware-name = "qcom/sm8250/lenovo/tb371fc/a650_zap.mbn";
+	};
 };
 
 &i2c1 {
@@ -725,8 +725,8 @@
 	vdda-supply = <&vreg_l9a_1p2>;
 	qcom,dual-dsi-mode;
 	qcom,sync-dual-dsi;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&mdss_dsi0_phy DSI_BYTE_PLL_CLK>,
-				 <&mdss_dsi0_phy DSI_PIXEL_PLL_CLK>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&mdss_dsi0_phy 0>,
+				 <&mdss_dsi0_phy 1>;
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
